{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n    The sequence is defined by P(1) = 1, P(2) = 1, and P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n - P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Cache to store computed values, initialized with base cases.\n    # This acts as the NewmanConway._cache from the design context.\n    memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    def _compute(k: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper function to recursively compute the kth term with memoization.\"\"\"\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        # Apply the recurrence relation for n > 2\n        p_n_minus_1 = _compute(k - 1)\n        result = _compute(p_n_minus_1) + _compute(k - p_n_minus_1)\n        \n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    # The design context's InputValidator is omitted due to the constraint\n    # \"Do NOT add isinstance() checks or raise exceptions for edge cases\".\n    return _compute(n)"}
