{"task_id": "Mbpp/90", "solution": "def len_log(items: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the length of the longest string in a list of strings.\n    If the input list is empty, it returns 0. Raises TypeError for non-string elements.\n    Compatibility: Python 3.6+ for type annotations.\n    Design decisions: Empty list returns 0; non-string elements raise TypeError (fail-fast).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not items:\n        return 0\n\n    for item in items:\n        if not isinstance(item, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the input list must be strings.\")\n\n    return max(len(s) for s in items)"}
