{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "def next_smallest_palindrome(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Public API. Returns the smallest integer palindrome strictly greater than n.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class IntegerInput:\n        \"\"\"Domain representation of the integer input.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, value: int):\n            self.value = value\n\n    class PalindromeResult:\n        \"\"\"Domain representation of the computed palindrome result.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, value: int):\n            self.value = value\n\n    class PalindromeCalculator:\n        \"\"\"Computes the next smallest palindrome strictly greater than a provided IntegerInput.\"\"\"\n\n        def is_palindrome(self, n: int) -> bool:\n            \"\"\"Returns True if the decimal representation of n is a palindrome.\n            Negative numbers are handled by their string representation.\n            \"\"\"\n            s = str(n)\n            return s == s[::-1]\n\n        def generate_next_palindrome(self, n: int) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Generates the smallest palindrome strictly greater than n.\"\"\"\n            # Start checking from the number strictly greater than n\n            candidate = n + 1\n            while not self.is_palindrome(candidate):\n                candidate += 1\n            return candidate\n\n        def next_smallest_palindrome(self, input_obj: IntegerInput) -> PalindromeResult:\n            \"\"\"Returns PalindromeResult containing the smallest palindrome strictly greater than input_obj.value.\"\"\"\n            next_pal = self.generate_next_palindrome(input_obj.value)\n            return PalindromeResult(next_pal)\n\n    calculator = PalindromeCalculator()\n    input_obj = IntegerInput(n)\n    result_obj = calculator.next_smallest_palindrome(input_obj)\n    return result_obj.value"}
