{"task_id": "Mbpp/290", "solution": "def max_length(lists):\n    \"\"\"Return (n, lst) where n is max len(sublist) and lst is one input sublist with length n.\"\"\"\n\n    def length_calc(lists):\n        \"\"\"Return list of lengths for each sublist in input order.\"\"\"\n        return [len(sublist) for sublist in lists]\n\n    def select_max(lists, lengths):\n        \"\"\"Return (n, lst) selecting first occurrence of max-length sublist.\"\"\"\n        if not lists:\n            return (0, []) # Handle empty input list of lists as per typical behavior\n        \n        max_len = 0\n        max_list = []\n        \n        # Iterate through lengths and lists simultaneously to find the first max\n        for i, current_len in enumerate(lengths):\n            if current_len > max_len:\n                max_len = current_len\n                max_list = lists[i]\n        \n        return (max_len, max_list)\n\n    if not lists:\n        return (0, [])\n\n    lengths = length_calc(lists)\n    return select_max(lists, lengths)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/287", "solution": "def validate_input(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates input: raises TypeError if n is not an int, ValueError if n is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an int\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be non-negative\")\n\ndef compute_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of squares of first n even natural numbers using a closed-form formula.\n    Returns 0 if n is 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    return (2 * n * (n + 1) * (2 * n + 1)) // 3\n\ndef square_Sum(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of squares of the first n even natural numbers.\n    It validates input and computes the sum using a closed-form formula.\n    \"\"\"\n    validate_input(n)\n    return compute_sum(n)"}
