{"task_id": "Mbpp/424", "solution": "```python\ndef extract_rear(tuple_of_strings):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the last character from each string in a tuple of strings.\n\n    Raises TypeError if input is not a tuple or elements are not strings.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple_of_strings, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for s in tuple_of_strings:\n        if not isinstance(s, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the tuple must be strings.\")\n        if not s:  # Handle empty strings, though design context implies non-empty by element[-1]\n            raise ValueError(\"String elements cannot be empty.\")\n        result.append(s[-1])\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/422", "solution": "class NaturalNumberSequence:\n    \"\"\"Helper class to generate a sequence of natural numbers.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, n: int) -> None:\n        self.n = n\n\n    def generateSequence(self) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Generates a list of natural numbers from 1 to n.\"\"\"\n        return list(range(1, self.n + 1))\n\nclass AverageCalculation:\n    \"\"\"Helper class to compute the sum of cubes and their average.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        pass\n\n    def computeAverageOfCubes(self, sequence: list[int]) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Computes the average of cubes for a given sequence of numbers.\"\"\"\n        if not sequence:\n            return 0.0 # Or raise an error, but design implies n >= 1\n        \n        sum_of_cubes = sum(x**3 for x in sequence)\n        return float(sum_of_cubes) / len(sequence)\n\n    def compute(self, sum_of_cubes: int, n: int) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the average given the sum of cubes and count.\"\"\"\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0.0\n        return float(sum_of_cubes) / n\n\ndef find_Average_Of_Cube(n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the average of cubes of the first n natural numbers.\n    This function orchestrates sequence generation and average calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    # According to the final strict instruction \"Do NOT add isinstance() checks or raise exceptions for edge cases\",\n    # input validation for n >= 1 and type(n) == int is omitted here.\n    \n    seq_gen = NaturalNumberSequence(n)\n    sequence = seq_gen.generateSequence()\n    \n    calc = AverageCalculation()\n    average = calc.computeAverageOfCubes(sequence)\n    \n    return average"}
