{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "def count_reverse_pairs(strings: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of reverse strings in the given list according to design rules.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Private helper function as per design\n    def _is_reverse(a: str, b: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if string b is the exact reverse of string a (case-sensitive).\"\"\"\n        return b == a[::-1]\n\n    # Domain class: InputList\n    class InputList:\n        def __init__(self, items: list[str]) -> None:\n            # Type validation removed as per output constraints (\"Do NOT add isinstance() checks\").\n            self.items = list(items)\n\n        def __len__(self) -> int:\n            return len(self.items)\n\n        def __getitem__(self, index: int) -> str:\n            return self.items[index]\n\n    # Domain class: StringItem (as per design, though not directly instantiated in the current counting loop)\n    class StringItem:\n        def __init__(self, value: str, index: int) -> None:\n            self.value = value\n            self.index = index\n\n    # Domain class: ReversePair (instantiated for diagnostics/future use, but not stored)\n    class ReversePair:\n        def __init__(self, index1: int, index2: int, str1: str, str2: str) -> None:\n            self.index1 = index1\n            self.index2 = index2\n            self.str1 = str1\n            self.str2 = str2\n\n    # Domain class: ReversePairCounter\n    class ReversePairCounter:\n        def countReversePairs(self, input_list: InputList) -> int:\n            \"\"\"\n            Counts unordered reverse-string index-pairs (i < j) in the InputList.\n            \"\"\"\n            count = 0\n            n = len(input_list)\n\n            for i in range(n):\n                str_i = input_list[i]\n                for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                    str_j = input_list[j]\n                    if _is_reverse(str_i, str_j):\n                        # Create ReversePair for diagnostics/future use as specified by design.\n                        ReversePair(i, j, str_i, str_j)\n                        count += 1\n            return count\n\n    # --- Public API function implementation (count_reverse_pairs) ---\n\n    # Input validation (e.g., isinstance checks, raising TypeError) is excluded\n    # as per output constraints (\"Do NOT add isinstance() checks or raise exceptions for edge cases\").\n    # The function trusts the `strings: list[str]` type hint.\n\n    # Handle lists shorter than two elements (BR-5).\n    if len(strings) < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    # Construct InputList from the provided strings.\n    input_list = InputList(strings)\n\n    # Invoke ReversePairCounter to perform the counting logic.\n    counter = ReversePairCounter()\n    result = counter.countReversePairs(input_list)\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/760", "solution": "def unique_Element(lst: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list of numbers contains only one distinct element.\n    Raises TypeError if input is not a list or contains non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    def validate_input(input_list: list) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Validates that the input is a list and all elements are numbers.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n        for element in input_list:\n            if not isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n                raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be numbers (int or float).\")\n        return True\n\n    def compute_distinct_count(input_list: list) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the number of distinct elements in the list.\"\"\"\n        return len(set(input_list))\n\n    validate_input(lst)\n    distinct_count = compute_distinct_count(lst)\n    return distinct_count == 1"}
